## Non-negotiable rules

> Seeded portable rules — specialize and ADD domain rules (currency, auth, calculations, etc.).

1. No `print`/`console.log` in application code — structured logging only. *(verify.sh)*
2. Exactly one error envelope; never fabricate success on failure (no `except → return []` HTTP 200). *(verify.sh + review)*
3. All datastore/external access goes through the designated wrapper; raw clients are banned. *(verify.sh)*
4. Enforce domain invariants at the schema/type layer, not just at runtime. *(schema constraints + CI)*
5. File-size budget: no file over {{MAX_FILE_LINES:-400}} lines (baseline exceptions in `scripts/.baseline-large-files.txt`). *(verify.sh)*
6. Auth uses random server-stored session tokens, never credentials-as-token. *(review + test)*
7. Every architectural decision gets an ADR before merge. *(review gate)*
8. Never run destructive/irreversible commands without explicit confirmation. *(guard-destructive.sh PreToolUse hook)*
9. One source of truth per concern (status, version, config); cross-link, don't duplicate. *(review)*
10. Every fixed incident produces a mechanical guard (hook/constraint/check), not just a doc note. *(feedback loop)*
11. No value that lives in code is hand-copied into prose docs — generate it or omit it. *(check-doc-freshness.sh)*
12. One naming convention for cycles/branches/versions/commits (see "Naming" below). *(commit-msg.sh + branch CI check)*
13. The fast test subset includes critical-path tests; the default scope never excludes a test dir. *(CI runs full scope)*
14. Recurring failure classes get promoted from `docs/known-issues.md` into `verify.sh` when automatable. *(feedback loop)*
15. {{DOMAIN_RULE_1 — e.g. "All monetary values stored in <base currency>; convert at the boundary."}}
16. {{DOMAIN_RULE_2}}

