## Naming convention (locked — synonyms banned)

| Level | Word | ID | Example |
|-------|------|----|---------|
| Initiative | Program | noun slug | "{{EXAMPLE_PROGRAM}}" |
| Track | Workstream | capital letter | A, B, C |
| Chunk | Step | letter+number | A1, B2 |
| Sub-unit | Task | decimal | A1.1 |

- Branch: `<feat\|chore\|fix\|claude>/<workstream><step>[-slug]`
- Commit: `<type>(<scope>): <imperative>` — scope = module/doc category, never a planning unit
- Plan file: `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<workstream><step>-<slug>.md`
- Version: semver — major=program · minor=shipped workstream/step · patch=hotfix only

---

## Verification Protocol

**Before marking any task complete, run `bash scripts/verify.sh` and fix all failures.**

| Exit | Meaning | Action |
|------|---------|--------|
| 0 | clean | safe to commit |
| 1 | safety violation | STOP — fix first, do not commit |
| 2 | logic violation | fix before committing |
| 3 | quality only | may commit; note what's flagged and why |

Pre-existing violations live in `scripts/.baseline-*.txt` (each with a justification comment). The gate
blocks only NEW violations; ratchet the baseline down over time.

Full session workflow: [`agent-handoff.md`] — orient → verify → work → sync docs → verify again.
